tus":"Confirmed"},{"personId":1630180,"position":"SF","lastName":"Bey","firstName":"Saddiq","status":"Confirmed"},{"personId":1630529,"position":"SG","lastName":"Jones","firstName":"Herbert","status":"Confirmed"},{"personId":1642847,"position":"PG","lastName":"Fears","firstName":"Jeremiah","status":"Confirmed"}]},"awayTeam":{"teamId":1610612763,"teamName":"Grizzlies","teamCity":"Memphis","teamTricode":"MEM","teamSlug":"grizzlies","wins":8,"losses":4,"score":142,"seed":0,"inBonus":null,"timeoutsRemaining":1,"groupWins":1,"groupLosses":1,"periods":[{"period":1,"periodType":"REGULAR","score":35},{"period":2,"periodType":"REGULAR","score":35},{"period":3,"periodType":"REGULAR","score":35},{"period":4,"periodType":"REGULAR","score":37}],"starters":[{"personId":1629660,"position":"PG","lastName":"Jerome","firstName":"Ty","status":"Confirmed"},{"personId":1630191,"position":"C","lastName":"Stewart","firstName":"Isaiah","status":"Confirmed"},{"personId":1642377,"position":"SF","lastName":"Wells","firstName":"Jaylen","status":"Confirmed"},{"personId":1642907,"position":"SG","lastName":"Coward","firstName":"Cedric","status":"Confirmed"},{"personId":1643409,"position":"PF","lastName":"Boozer","firstName":"Cameron","status":"Confirmed"}]},"reportModules":[{"moduleType":"game_header","order":0},{"moduleType":"defining_moments","order":1},{"moduleType":"top_performers","order":2},{"moduleType":"shot_difficulty","order":3},{"moduleType":"gravity_spotlight","order":4},{"moduleType":"defensive_spotlight","order":5},{"moduleType":"leverage_spotlight","order":6}],"gameOverview":{"title":"The Memphis Grizzlies Earn the Win","body":"The Memphis Grizzlies defeated the New Orleans Pelicans 142-111. Saddiq Bey led the Pelicans with 30 points on 11-for-20 shooting, including 6-for-9 from three-point range, and grabbed 10 rebounds. Zion Williamson added 22 points on 7-for-15 from the field for New Orleans. For Memphis, Jerami Grant scored 22 points on efficient 7-for-10 shooting with 3-for-6 from beyond the arc, while Ty Jerome contributed 17 points and 9 assists in the Grizzlies' dominant performance.\n\nThe Pelicans built early momentum and mounted a 13–2 run during the third quarter to stay competitive. However, Memphis seized control down the stretch with a decisive 16–2 run in the fourth quarter that put the game out of reach. Taylor Hendricks knocked down a three-pointer, making it 126–103 in favor of the Grizzlies with 4:09 remaining in the fourth. The Memphis Grizzlies paired a substantial advantage in bench scoring with an edge in second-chance scoring over the New Orleans Pelicans.\n\nBey drew above-expected defensive pressure with an Average Gravity of 16.5, commanding attention throughout the contest. His overall impact registered a Total Leverage of 2.2. Grant's efficiency stood out on the other end, shooting 19.2 percentage points above expectation on his seven made field goals."}},"defining_moments":{"gameId":"0022600038","moduleType":"defining_moments","definingMoments":[{"guid":"b08e8597-897f-ffe1-0898-e82dd27d815c","rank":1,"title":"Taylor Hendricks Delivers a Triple","summary":"Taylor Hendricks converted a three-pointer off the assist from Cam Spencer, making it 126–103 in favor of the Grizzlies with 4:09 remaining in the fourth.","category":"Scoring","eventNum":682,"largeHls":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/13/0022600038/682/b08e8597-897f-ffe1-0898-e82dd27d815c_hls_3500kbps_1280x720.m3u8","largeUrl":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/13/0022600038/682/b08e8597-897f-ffe1-0898-e82dd27d815c_1280x720.mp4","playerId":1641707,"smallHls":"","smallUrl":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/13/0022600038/682/b08e8597-897f-ffe1-0898-e82dd27d815c_320x180.mp4","mediumHls":"","mediumUrl":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/13/0022600038/682/b08e8597-897f-ffe1-0898-e82dd27d815c_960x540.mp4","playListUrl":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/13/0022600038/682/b08e8597-897f-ffe1-0898-e82dd27d815c.